  {
    "slideType": "INSTRUCTIONS",
    "content": "INSTRUCTIONS FOR THE PSYCH TEST\n\nGreetings of the Day.\n\nToday you will undergo a set of psychological tests designed to understand your natural way of thinking, feeling, acting, and dealing with situations. These tests are not school examinations and there are no fixed right or wrong answers. You need not compare yourself with others. Every individual is likely to react in his/her own way.\n\nDo not try to project an artificial personality or write what you think the Board wants to see. The tests are designed to study spontaneity and consistency. Therefore, your first natural response is usually more useful than an overthought response.\n\nThe Psych Test battery consists of four different tests\n\nThematic Apperception Test (TAT)\n\nWord Association Test (WAT)\n\nSituation Reaction Test (SRT)\n\nSelf Description\n\nInstructions for each test will be flashed on the screen for 3 minutes prior commencement of that test. Read the instructions carefully. They are self-explanatory. Manage your time sensibly and attempt every test with full involvement. Even if one response does not go well, do not carry it forward mentally into the next test.\n\nRemain calm, write legibly, and express yourself freely. We are not searching for perfection; we are trying to understand your personality.\n\nAll the best.",
    "displayTime": 180,
    "order": 1,
    "module": "INTRO"
  },
  {
    "slideType": "INSTRUCTIONS",
    "content": "THEMATIC APPERCEPTION TEST (TAT)",
    "displayTime": 10,
    "order": 2,
    "module": "TAT"
  },
  {
    "slideType": "INSTRUCTIONS",
    "content": "This is a test of your imagination. In this test you will be shown several pictures one after the other. What you are required to do is write a story around the picture and the characters shown in the picture, covering\n\na. What led to the situation (PAST)\n\nb. What is going on (PRESENT)\n\nc. What will be the outcome (FUTURE)\n\nYou will also describe the feelings, thoughts and actions of the characters shown in the picture.\n\nIn total you will be shown 11 pictures, and 12th picture will be a blank slide wherein you are free to imagine a picture of your own choice and then write a story around that picture which you have imagined.\n\nEach picture will be shown for 30 seconds, and you will be given 04 minutes to write the story\n\nOnce the picture goes off the screen, you may start writing the story for four minutes and once four minutes are over the next picture will automatically be flashed on the screen.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR TAT",
    "displayTime": 180,
    "order": 3,
    "module": "TAT"
  },
